  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-10-27T04:25:41.313Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In PCVR, a world gimmick that appears to use Input.GetKey, the quest A and X buttons do not react, but the B and Y buttons do when pressed.\n\nConfirmed by VirtualDesktop and Airlink.\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/1061679297171042304/1167312121504215071/PXL_20231027_035957729.TS2.mp4?ex=654dab21&is=653b3621&hm=c0476bd668bf8c014cc2ff4b6e7df020b22e027476723c46cd11aaf536a658df&\n\nThis is a video of the symptoms.\n\nThe operation assigned to Oculus R Button A (Turn signal Right,Here, \"ウィンカー右\" is indicated in Japanese.) is reacting to Button B.\n\nIf you get into the car and perform the operations assigned to these buttons, and then get out and get back in, the car system will stop working and will not accept any operations.\n\nThe controls built into VRChat, such as jumping and microphone on/off, work fine. The only thing that seems to be affected is the world gimmick.",
